  "narrative": "The newly delivered independent validation for H41 decisively supports the PTEN-loss association with stronger STAT3 dependency in this dataset. Because estimates are already signed to the registered direction (-1, i.e., stronger STAT3 dependency), the discovery contrast was +0.267, 95% CI [0.215,0.319], and the independent validation contrast was +0.268 with a stringent independent interval [0.188,0.348]. Both point estimates are almost identical, and the validation lower bound remains far above zero and far above any plausible 10%-scale threshold for the STAT3 score distribution. In raw terms, PTEN-loss lines show substantially more negative STAT3 dependency scores, and this difference is large relative to the STAT3 mean and SD. I therefore accept H41 as a scientifically meaningful dataset association and close direct follow-up on the main effect. This remains an association, not causal evidence or a clinical generalizability claim. I keep H3 unresolved but deferred because its independent validation point estimate was near zero and imprecise, with the interval still spanning both the null and potentially meaningful effects; it is not compelling enough for further immediate validation. The next analyses should focus on registered context tests around the accepted effects, especially H44-H46 for whether the PTEN-STAT3 effect is modified by lineage subtype or PIK3CA biology, H47 for RB1-POLR2A subtype context, and the broad untested coverage claims H14-H19 and H24-H31. If PTEN-STAT3 context interactions are near null, the accepted effect appears stable across these measured contexts; if they are large, they should be followed up cautiously without causal interpretation.",
  "research_notes": "Round-3 synthesize. Accepted/validated dataset associations: H6 SMARCA4 loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency (signed +0.784 CI 0.765-0.803); H7 MSI-high -> stronger WRN dependency (signed +0.790 CI 0.760-0.819); H13 KEAP1 loss -> weaker NFE2L2 dependency (signed +0.796 CI 0.776-0.816); H41 PTEN loss -> stronger STAT3 dependency, now independently validated (discovery signed +0.267 CI 0.215-0.319; validation signed +0.268 independent interval 0.188-0.348), investigation closed. H3 EGFR amplification -> EGFR dependency remains unresolved but deferred after weak/inconclusive independent validation. H39 RB1 loss -> POLR2A is borderline and remains active. Next priorities: analyze already registered H44-H47 PTEN-STAT3 and RB1-POLR2A context tests plus untested broad coverage H14-H19 and H24-H31; avoid spending validation on H3 unless context evidence makes it informative. Do not infer causality or clinical generalizability from these associations."
}

