  "narrative": "I interpreted every signed estimate as reported: a positive signed value supports the registered hypothesis direction, while a negative signed value contradicts it. The strongest new evidence confirms that the accepted main-effect associations are not confined to the full sample and do not appear to be simple artifacts of the most obvious co-alteration contexts. H48, PTEN loss versus STAT3 dependency among TP53-intact lines, has signed mean_difference +0.287, 95% CI [0.227,0.347]. This is far larger than an approximate 10% scale change for the STAT3 score distribution and far away from zero, so I accept it and close direct follow-up. H46, PTEN loss among PIK3CA-intact lines, is similarly large: +0.267, CI [0.210,0.323]. Together with H48, this strongly suggests that the accepted PTEN-loss association with stronger STAT3 dependency is not explained only by TP53 co-loss or PIK3CA-mutant context, although co-alteration structure and technical confounding remain possible. H49, SMARCA4 loss among ARID1A-intact lines, remains enormous: +0.777, CI [0.756,0.798], supporting specificity of the SMARCA4-loss association for SMARCA2 dependency rather than a broad SWI/SNF effect, because ARID1A loss alone was not supported. H50, MSI-high among TP53-intact lines, remains enormous: +0.780, CI [0.747,0.813], so the MSI-high WRN association is robust to TP53 co-loss in this dataset. H51, KEAP1 loss among STK11-intact lines, is +0.801, CI [0.779,0.823], reinforcing the accepted reversed NFE2L2 direction: KEAP1 loss is associated with less negative, hence weaker, NFE2L2 dependency. For NFE2L2 the mean score is close to zero, so a 10% relative threshold is not the best guide, but the absolute interval is very large relative to the score SD and is not compatible with a trivial effect.\n\nThe modifier tests are less informative. H44, adenocarcinoma interaction for PTEN-STAT3, is centered near zero, +0.001, CI [-0.115,0.117]. This provides no evidence that the PTEN effect 