ct context; and KEAP1-NFE2L2 survives STK11-intact context. The most useful unresolved candidate is RB1 loss for POLR2A dependency, especially H39, because both the overall estimate and H56 are near a threshold and imprecise. I therefore request independent validation of H39. I also registered batch-robustness proposals for the strongest accepted associations because screen batch could contribute to dependencies or to predictor distribution; if these effects persist within batch_a, technical batch confounding becomes less plausible, although this still would remain a dataset association and not a causal or generalizable claim.",
