  "narrative": "All proposals are interpreted using the signed-estimate convention: for direction -1, a positive reported estimate corresponds to a raw negative exposed-minus-comparator shift, meaning the exposed group has more negative dependency scores and stronger dependency; for direction +1, a positive reported estimate corresponds to a raw positive shift, meaning less negative scores and weaker dependency.  The first block refines accepted dataset associations in co-mutation contexts that are biologically plausible but not yet fully tested. KEAP1 loss and KRAS mutation frequently co-occur in lung adenocarcinoma biology, so I split the accepted KEAP1-to-NFE2L2 weaker-dependency association by KRAS mutation status. If the large positive signed effect persists in both KRAS-mutant and KRAS-wildtype lines, the association is less dependent on KRAS co-alteration; if it collapses in one context, the claim would need a narrower context interpretation. SMARCA4-loss-to-SMARCA2-stronger-dependency is already robust by library, ARID1A context, and independent validation, but testing KRAS-mutant and TP53-loss strata can clarify whether this effect is diluted by other common driver contexts. PTEN-loss-to-STAT3-stronger-dependency has been accepted in TP53-intact, PIK3CA-intact, TP53-loss, PIK3CA-mutant, and Avana-library strata; adding KRAS-mutant lines tests whether the effect remains in another major driver background. MSI-high-to-WRN-stronger-dependency is validated and robust in Avana and TP53-intact lines; the proposed TP53-loss stratum complements that, though exposed cells may be smaller and therefore less precise.  The MYC-amplification-to-RPL11 test is mechanistically motivated but not yet supported. MYC amplification can increase translational and ribosomal stress, and this may create stronger ribosomal dependency preferentially when TP53 is intact. A near-null or reversed result would leave MYC amplification unsupported as a useful RPL11 predictor in this dataset.  The remaining proposals broaden coverage of underresolved dependencies. PIK3CA mutation could bypass KRAS pathway dependency by activating downstream signaling, so I test whether PIK3CA-mutant lines have weaker KRAS dependency; direction +1 means stronger signed support when KRAS dependency scores are less negative. Conversely, STK11 loss among KRAS-mutant lines may alter metabolic stress and could be associated with stronger KRAS dependency; direction -1 means positive signed support corresponds to more negative KRAS dependency. Finally, KRAS-mutant lines may be less dependent on ERBB2 because they use a mutually exclusive or bypass oncogenic driver; direction +1 means positive signed support corresponds to less negative ERBB2 dependency.  These new tests are exploratory association tests, not causal claims or generalizable clinical claims. They should be accepted only if intervals exclude zero and the signed effect is large enough relative to each outcome's score distribution to be scientifically meaningful, with near-zero small effects treated as non-supportive. Low-priority duplicate or redundant active claims were reduced in the assessments to make space for the accepted-effect subtype and batch robustness tests, especially H14, H15, H63, H64, and H58-H61, along with the most informative new stratified and pathway-bypass tests above.",
  "research_notes": "Round-5 explore update. Accepted/validated main dataset associations: SMARCA4 loss with stronger SMARCA2 dependency; MSI-high with stronger WRN dependency; PTEN loss with stronger STAT3 dependency; KEAP1 loss with weaker NFE2L2 dependency accepted on discovery and robust stratum evidence. Validated accepted main effects include H6, H7, and H41; KEAP1-NFE2L2 main H13 still lacks its own independent validation but is robust in Avana, STK11-intact, STK11-loss, and other strata. Low-priority or redundant EGFR amplification, RB1-loss, ERBB2 interaction, ARID1A interaction, and PTEN/KEAP1 interaction follow-ups were closed or deferred where redundant. New proposed priorities: context-specific robustness of accepted effects in KRAS-mutant, KRAS-wildtype, TP53-loss, and PIK3CA-intact/TP53-intact contexts; MYC-RPL11 in TP53-intact lines; pathway bypass/co-dependency hypotheses for KRAS dependency with PIK3CA and STK11, and ERBB2 dependency with KRAS. Next analyze should still include adenocarcinoma subtype robustness for accepted effects H14/H15/H63/H64 and, if capacity allows, batch_a robustness H58-H61. Validation capacity remains 6; H13 KEAP1-NFE2L2 is the best remaining candidate for voluntary validation if subtype/co-mutation robustness continues. All conclusions remain supplied-dataset associations, not causal or clinical."
