port MYC amplification versus stronger RPL11 dependency in TP53-intact lines: signed estimate -0.009, CI [-0.034,0.015]. The point estimate is negative and the upper bound is too small to represent a clinically meaningful positive shift on the RPL11 score scale, so I reject the registered direction and close it. H15, H61, H63, and H64 complete subtype and batch robustness checks and all support accepted effects: MSI-high WRN dependency in adenocarcinoma +0.784, CI [0.748,0.820]; KEAP1 NFE2L2 in batch_a +0.812, CI [0.765,0.858]; KEAP1 NFE2L2 in adenocarcinoma +0.793, CI [0.769,0.817]; and PTEN STAT3 in adenocarcinoma +0.268, CI [0.206,0.330]. The multiplicity is substantial, but these are not borderline findings for the accepted effects: they are large, consistently signed, and lower bounds are far above trivial. The main remaining scientific weakness is that the KEAP1-NFE2L2 main claim, H13, still lacks its own independent validation despite very strong discovery and stratum robustness. I therefore request independent validation of H13.",
