  "narrative": "All estimates were interpreted as already signed to the registered hypothesis direction. For direction -1 claims, a positive estimate means stronger dependency in the exposed group; for direction +1 claims, a positive estimate means weaker dependency in the exposed group. H13 now has independent validation in addition to discovery: signed estimate +0.796, 95% CI [0.776,0.816], and independent validation +0.791, independent interval [0.763,0.820]. This is a very large shift on the NFE2L2 dependency-score scale, where the full-sample mean is approximately -0.093 and SD is approximately 0.363, and it is far above any 10% practical threshold. Direction +1 means KEAP1-loss lines have less negative NFE2L2 scores, hence weaker NFE2L2 dependency. I therefore reaffirm and close H13. H7 also has validation: discovery +0.790, CI [0.760,0.819], validation +0.812, independent interval [0.765,0.858]. This is far above the WRN score SD of approximately 0.263 and supports MSI-high being associated with stronger WRN dependency in this dataset. I reaffirm and close H7. H39 failed to provide meaningful support: validation estimate was +0.00019, independent interval [-0.038,0.039], near null for RB1 loss versus POLR2A dependency. The interval is not precise enough to exclude every clinically meaningful positive effect, but there is no positive evidence that RB1 loss is associated with stronger POLR2A dependency. I leave it unresolved and closed. Overall, the strongest supported dataset associations are SMARCA4 loss with stronger SMARCA2 dependency, MSI-high with stronger WRN dependency, PTEN loss with stronger STAT3 dependency, and KEAP1 loss with weaker NFE2L2 dependency; all now have discovery plus independent validation. Several other candidates were unsupported or failed replication, including EGFR amplification with EGFR dependency, RB1 loss with POLR2A dependency, BRAF V600E, ERBB2 amplification, and MYC-related dependency effects in several contexts. These remain