  "narrative": "All estimates are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction. For direction -1 claims, a positive signed estimate means the exposed group has a more negative dependency score and therefore stronger dependency. For direction +1 claims, a positive signed estimate means a less negative dependency score and therefore weaker dependency. H6 was reassessed because the independent validation response deadline arrived. R53 gave signed estimate +0.804 with independent interval [0.775, 0.833], replicating the discovery estimate +0.784 [0.765, 0.803]. Both intervals are entirely positive, the validation lower bound is far above zero, and the effect is very large relative to the SMARCA2 score distribution, about 2.2 SD. This strongly supports the dataset association that SMARCA4 loss is associated with stronger SMARCA2 dependency. I reaffirm and close H6. H83 was the requested validation of the TP53-loss stratum for MSI-high versus stronger WRN dependency. R79 gave signed estimate +0.760 with independent interval [0.674, 0.847], while discovery R60 was +0.833 [0.765, 0.900]. Despite the smaller exposed cell in the validation split, the independent interval remains positive and far above zero; this supports the accepted stratum-specific association in this dataset, although precision is lower than in the full population. I reaffirm and close H83. H21 tested whether ARID1A loss alone is associated with stronger SMARCA2 dependency. Discovery R15 was negative and small under the registered direction: -0.017 [ -0.057, 0.023]. The new validation R80 is near null and also negative in signed terms: -0.002 [ -0.062, 0.058]. Neither point estimate supports the registered positive direction. The validation interval is wide enough that I do not claim a precisely zero ARID1A effect, but the original claim was a clinically meaningful positive stronger-dependency association, and the combined evidence does not support it. I keep H21 rejected and closed. Overall, the 